<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="NAM" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Nahum</para>

<para style="toc1">Nahum</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="NAM 1"/>

<para style="s">The Burden against Nineveh</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="NAM 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Jonah 1:1–3</char></note>The burden of Nineveh, the book of the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite: <verse eid="NAM 1:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="NAM 1:2"/>A God jealous and avenging <char style="add">is</char> YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:2">avenging <char style="add">is</char> YHWH and owner of fury; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:2">avenging <char style="add">is</char> YHWH on His adversaries, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:2">and He is watching for His enemies. <verse eid="NAM 1:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="NAM 1:3"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> slow to anger </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:3">and great in power; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:3">and YHWH does not entirely acquit. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:3">In the whirlwind and in the storm <char style="add">is</char> His way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:3">and the clouds <char style="add">are</char> the dust of His feet. <verse eid="NAM 1:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="NAM 1:4"/>He rebukes the sea and makes it dry, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:4">and all the rivers He dries up; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:4">Bashan and Carmel wither; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:4">the flower of Lebanon has withered. <verse eid="NAM 1:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="NAM 1:5"/>The mountains quake before Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:5">and the hills melt, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:5">and the earth lifts up before His face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:5">and the world and all those dwelling in it. <verse eid="NAM 1:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="NAM 1:6"/>Before the face of His indignation, who can stand? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:6">And who can stand up in the burning of His anger? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:6">His fury is poured out like the fire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:6">and the rocks are torn down by Him. <verse eid="NAM 1:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="NAM 1:7"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> good </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:7">for a stronghold in the day of distress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:7">and He knows those taking refuge in Him. <verse eid="NAM 1:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="NAM 1:8"/>And with an overflowing flood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:8">He will make a complete end of her place,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Nineveh</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:8">and His enemies will pursue darkness. <verse eid="NAM 1:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="NAM 1:9"/>What are you⁺ plotting against YHWH? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:9">He will make a complete end; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:9">distress will not rise up a second time. <verse eid="NAM 1:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="NAM 1:10"/>For as with thorns, they will be entangled, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:10">and like their drink becoming drunk, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:10">they are consumed like stubble fully dry. <verse eid="NAM 1:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="NAM 1:11"/>From you came forth </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:11">one devising evil plots against YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:11">a counselor of wickedness. <verse eid="NAM 1:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="NAM 1:12"/>Thus says YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:12">“Though they are full and likewise numerous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:12">so will they be cut down and will pass away. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:12">And I have afflicted you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:12">I will afflict you no more. <verse eid="NAM 1:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="NAM 1:13"/>And now I will break off his yoke from upon you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:13">and your bonds I will tear away.” <verse eid="NAM 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="NAM 1:14"/>And YHWH has given a command concerning you: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:14">“No longer </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:14">will be sown forth of your name; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:14">from the house of your gods I will cut off </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:14">the carved image and the molten image; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:14">I will dig your grave, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:14">for you are of little account.” <verse eid="NAM 1:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="NAM 1:15"/>Behold, on the mountains, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:15">the feet of one bringing good news, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:15">announcing peace. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:15">Celebrate, O Judah, your feasts; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:15">fulfill your vows; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 1:15">for the worthless one will continue no more to pass through you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 1:15">all of him has been cut off! <verse eid="NAM 1:15"/></para>

<chapter eid="NAM 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="NAM 2"/>

<para style="s">The Overthrow of Nineveh</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="NAM 2:1"/>The one scattering has come up </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:1">before your face; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:1">guard the fortress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:1">watch over the road; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:1">strengthen your loins, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:1">strengthen <char style="add">your</char> power greatly! <verse eid="NAM 2:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="NAM 2:2"/>For YHWH will restore the majesty of Jacob, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:2">like the majesty of Israel, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:2">for those emptying have emptied them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:2">and have ruined their branches. <verse eid="NAM 2:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="NAM 2:3"/>The shields of his mighty men are red; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:3">the men of valor are clothed in scarlet; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:3">with fire of burning steel the chariots <char style="add">come</char> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:3">on the day of his preparing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:3">and the cypresses quiver.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the spears of cypress are brandished</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; alternately, the spears may be of </char><char style="fq" closed="false">pine</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">juniper</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">fir</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; LXX and Syriac </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they are prepared, and the horsemen rush to and fro.</char></note> <verse eid="NAM 2:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="NAM 2:4"/>Through the streets the chariots dash; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:4">they rush around in the squares; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:4">their appearance <char style="add">is</char> like torches, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:4">like the lightning they run! <verse eid="NAM 2:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="NAM 2:5"/>He summons his nobles, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:5">they stumble in their walk; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:5">they hurry <char style="add">to</char> her wall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:5">and the siege-cover is prepared. <verse eid="NAM 2:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="NAM 2:6"/>The gates of the rivers are opened, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:6">and the palace is dissolved. <verse eid="NAM 2:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="NAM 2:7"/>And it is established: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:7">She shall be ncovered <char style="add">and</char> brought up, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:7">and her maidservants will be moaning as the voice of doves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:7">beating on their breasts. <verse eid="NAM 2:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="NAM 2:8"/>And Nineveh <char style="add">was</char> like a pool of water, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:8">from the days of her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:8">and they flee: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:8">“Stand, stand,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:8">and no one is turning back. <verse eid="NAM 2:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="NAM 2:9"/>“Plunder the silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:9">plunder the gold!” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:9">And there is no end to the provision—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:9">the worth of every precious article. <verse eid="NAM 2:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="NAM 2:10"/>Emptiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:10">an empty place and laid waste! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:10">The heart melts, and the knees shake, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:10">and <char style="add">there is</char> anguish in all loins, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:10">and the faces of all of them are gathered to paleness! <verse eid="NAM 2:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="NAM 2:11"/>Where <char style="add">is</char> the dwelling of the lions, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:11">and the feeding place that <char style="add">was</char> unto the young lions—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:11">where there walked the lion <char style="add">and</char> lioness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:11"><char style="add">and</char> the cub of the lion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:11">and nothing made them afraid? <verse eid="NAM 2:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="NAM 2:12"/>The lion was tearing enough for his cubs, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:12">and strangling for his lionesses; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:12">and he filled his caves <char style="add">with</char> prey, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:12">and his dens with flesh. <verse eid="NAM 2:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="NAM 2:13"/>“Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:13">a declaration of YHWH of Hosts, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:13">“And I will burn in smoke your chariots, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:13">and the sword will devour your young lions; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 2:13">and I will cut off your prey from the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:13">and will be heard no more </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 2:13">the voice of your messengers!” <verse eid="NAM 2:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="NAM 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="NAM 3"/>

<para style="s">Judgment on Nineveh</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="NAM 3:1"/>Woe <char style="add">to</char> the city of bloodshed. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:1">All of it <char style="add">is</char> a lie, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:1">full of plunder—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:1"><char style="add">its</char> prey does not depart— <verse eid="NAM 3:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="NAM 3:2"/>the voice of the whip, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:2">the voice of the rattling of the wheel, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:2">with galloping horse </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:2">and bounding chariot! <verse eid="NAM 3:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="NAM 3:3"/>Horsemen <char style="add">are</char> ascending </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:3">with a flame of sword </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:3">and flashing of spear, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:3">and the abundance of the slain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:3">and the mass of the corpse—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:3">there is no end to the bodies—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:3">and they stumble over the bodies. <verse eid="NAM 3:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="NAM 3:4"/>From the abundance of prostitutions of the prostitute, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:4">fine of favor, the mistress of sorcery, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:4">the one selling nations by her prostitution, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:4">and families by her sorcery. <verse eid="NAM 3:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="NAM 3:5"/>“Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:5">a declaration of YHWH of Hosts, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:5">“And I will uncover your skirts over your face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:5">and I will let see the nations your nakedness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:5">and the kingdoms your shame. <verse eid="NAM 3:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="NAM 3:6"/>And I will cast upon you abominations </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:6">and I will treat you with contempt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:6">and I will set you as a spectacle! <verse eid="NAM 3:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="NAM 3:7"/>And it will come to pass <char style="add">that</char> all seeing you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:7">will flee from you, and will say, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:7">‘Nineveh is devastated. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:7">Who will bemoan for her?’ </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:7">From where should I seek </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:7">comforters for you?” <verse eid="NAM 3:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="NAM 3:8"/>Are you better than Thebes,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">than No-amon</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:8">the <char style="add">city</char> setting by the River, <char style="add">with</char> the waters around her, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:8">whose rampart <char style="add">was</char> the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:8"><char style="add">and</char> the sea her wall? <verse eid="NAM 3:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="NAM 3:9"/>Cush<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the upper Nile region</char></note> <char style="add">was</char> her strength, and Egypt, and there was no end; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:9">Libya and Lubim came to be for your help. <verse eid="NAM 3:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="NAM 3:10"/>Yet she <char style="add">was</char> as an exile; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:10">she went into captivity; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:10">even her infants were dashed to pieces </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:10">at the head of every street, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:10">and over her honored ones they cast lots, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:10">and all her great ones were bound in chains. <verse eid="NAM 3:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="NAM 3:11"/>Even you will become drunk; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:11">you will be hidden; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:11">you will even seek refuge from the enemy. <verse eid="NAM 3:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="NAM 3:12"/>All your fortresses are fig trees </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:12">with the first ripe figs; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:12">if they are shaken, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:12">they fall into the mouth of the one eating. <verse eid="NAM 3:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="NAM 3:13"/>Behold, your people </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:13"><char style="add">are</char> women in your midst; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:13">the gates of your land are wide open to your enemies; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:13">fire has devoured your bars. <verse eid="NAM 3:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="NAM 3:14"/>Draw for yourself water for the siege; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:14">strengthen your fortresses; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:14">Go into the clay and tread on the mortar; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:14">take hold or the brick kiln. <verse eid="NAM 3:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="NAM 3:15"/>There the fire will devour you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:15">the sword will cut you down; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:15">it will eat you up like the locust. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:15">Make yourself many like the young locust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:15">make yourself many like the swarming locust. <verse eid="NAM 3:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="NAM 3:16"/>You have multiplied your merchants </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:16">above the stars of the heavens; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:16">the young locust strips <char style="add">it</char> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:16">and flies away. <verse eid="NAM 3:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="NAM 3:17"/>Your princes<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">guards</char></note> <char style="add">are</char> like the swarming locust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:17">and your scribes<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">marshals</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">generals</char></note> like clouds of locusts of locusts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:17">those camping on the fences on a day of cold; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:17">the sun has risen, and it flees away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:17">and it is not known the place of it, where they <char style="add">are</char>. <verse eid="NAM 3:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="NAM 3:18"/>Your shepherds slumber, O king of Assyria; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:18">your nobles are at rest; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:18">your people are scattered on the mountains, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:18">and no one is gathering them. <verse eid="NAM 3:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="NAM 3:19"/>There is no easing of your injury; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:19">your wound is severe; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:19">all those hearing the report of you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:19">clap the hands over you. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="NAM 3:19">For upon whom has not your evil </para>

<para style="q2" vid="NAM 3:19">passed continually? <verse eid="NAM 3:19"/></para>

<chapter eid="NAM 3"/>

</usx>
